es3=12$.","En":"The common denominator is 12 because $6\\times2=12$ and $4\\times3=12$."},{"Ar":"نحوّل الكسرين إلى $\\frac{10}{12}$ و$\\frac3{12}$.","En":"Convert both fractions to $\\frac{10}{12}$ and $\\frac3{12}$."},{"Ar":"نطرح البسطين مع تثبيت المقام: $\\frac{10-3}{12}=\\frac7{12}$.","En":"Subtract numerators retaining the denominator: $\\frac{10-3}{12}=\\frac7{12}$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$\\frac7{12}$","En":"$\\frac7{12}$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تجمع أو تطرح المقامات.","En":"Do not add or subtract the denominators."},"FormulaLatex":"\\frac ab\\pm\\frac cd=\\frac{ad\\pm bc}{bd}\\quad(bd\\ne0)","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\frac56-\\frac14=\\frac{10}{12}-\\frac3{12}=\\frac7{12}$","En":"$\\frac56-\\frac14=\\frac{10}{12}-\\frac3{12}=\\frac7{12}$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\frac7{12}+\\frac14=\\frac{10}{12}=\\frac56$","En":"$\\frac7{12}+\\frac14=\\frac{10}{12}=\\frac56$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"إضافة $\\frac14$ إلى $\\frac49$ تعطي $\\frac{25}{36}$ وليس $\\frac56$.","En":"Adding $\\frac14$ to $\\frac49$ gives $\\frac{25}{36}$, not $\\frac56$."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"نصف زائد ربع يساوي ثلاثة أرباع، لا خمسة أسداس.","En":"One half plus one quarter is three quarters, not five sixths."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"3/12 هو الكسر المطروح نفسه بعد توحيد المقام وليس الفرق.","En":"3/12 is the converted subtrahend, not the difference."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$لجمع الكسور أو طرحها نوحد المقامات ثم نجمع أو نطرح البسوط.

$\frac ab\pm\frac cd=\frac{ad\pm bc}{bd}\quad(bd\ne0)$

1. المقام المشترك 12، لأن $6\times2=12$ و$4\times3=12$.

2. نحوّل الكسرين إلى $\frac{10}{12}$ و$\frac3{12}$.

3. نطرح البسطين مع تثبيت المقام: $\frac{10-3}{12}=\frac7{12}$.

$\frac56-\frac14=\frac{10}{12}-\frac3{12}=\frac7{12}$

$\frac7{12}$ بلا وحدة قياس

$\frac7{12}+\frac14=\frac{10}{12}=\frac56$

لا تجمع أو تطرح المقامات.$mw$,$mw$To add or subtract fractions, use a common denominator, then operate on the numerators.

$\frac ab\pm\frac cd=\frac{ad\pm bc}{bd}\quad(bd\ne0)$

1. The common denominator is 12 because $6\times2=12$ and $4\times3=12$.

2. Convert both fractions to $\frac{10}{12}$ and $\frac3{12}$.

3. Subtract numerators retaining the denominator: $\frac{10-3}{12}=\frac7{12}$.

$\frac56-\frac14=\frac{10}{12}-\frac3{12}=\frac7{12}$

$\frac7{12}$ Dimensionless

$\frac7{12}+\frac14=\frac{10}{12}=\frac56$

Do not add or subtract the denominators.$mw$),
